From: Ryan Hughes <ryan@heyoodle.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:20:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: quirks: let the NVIDIA N1x NVMe link reach L1.2 so the
 SoC can sleep

The N1x firmware leaves ASPM off on every PCIe link. In suspend-to-idle
the NVMe drive goes to D3hot (its port has StorageD3Enable), but with
PCI-PM L1.2 off the link sits in plain L1 with CLKREQ# asserted. The
SoC's power manager then records a PCIe wake about every 60 ms and never
gets past its shallowest platform idle level (MCUSYS off), so the laptop
draws 6-15 W asleep.

Allow ASPM L1 and PCI-PM L1.1/L1.2 on the NVMe link through
pci_enable_link_state(). The SoC then stays in DRIPS (PPS4, DRAM in
self-refresh) for the whole suspend: 0.77 W over a 7.3 h night on the
ASUS ProArt P14, woken only by the lid. ASPM L1.1/L1.2 while the drive is
active and clock power management stay off, as the firmware has them.

The platform is recognised by its platform extension device, NVDA6210.
---
 drivers/pci/quirks.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -5891,6 +5891,30 @@
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_CLASS_RESUME_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_NVIDIA, PCI_ANY_ID,
 			       PCI_BASE_CLASS_DISPLAY, 16, quirk_nvidia_hda);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_ACPI
+/*
+ * The NVIDIA N1x firmware leaves ASPM off on every PCIe link. In
+ * suspend-to-idle the NVMe drive goes to D3hot, but with PCI-PM L1.2 off its
+ * link sits in plain L1 with CLKREQ# asserted, and the SoC's power manager
+ * is woken by PCIe about every 60 ms, never getting past the shallowest
+ * platform idle level. With PCI-PM L1.1/L1.2 allowed, the SoC stays in its
+ * deepest state for the whole suspend and sleeps at under 1 W instead of
+ * 6-15 W. The platform is recognised by its PEP device, NVDA6210.
+ */
+static void quirk_n1x_nvme_l1ss(struct pci_dev *pdev)
+{
+	if (!acpi_dev_present("NVDA6210", NULL, -1))
+		return;
+
+	if (!pci_enable_link_state(pdev, PCIE_LINK_STATE_L1 |
+				   PCIE_LINK_STATE_L1_1_PCIPM |
+				   PCIE_LINK_STATE_L1_2_PCIPM))
+		pci_info(pdev, "N1x: allowing ASPM L1 and PCI-PM L1.1/L1.2\n");
+}
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_CLASS_FINAL(PCI_ANY_ID, PCI_ANY_ID,
+			      PCI_CLASS_STORAGE_EXPRESS, 0, quirk_n1x_nvme_l1ss);
+#endif
+
 /*
  * Some IDT switches incorrectly flag an ACS Source Validation error on
  * completions for config read requests even though PCIe r7.0, sec
